gned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(R)$ is ${{r}_{1},{r}_{2}}.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $B={{r}_{1},{r}_{2},{r}_{3}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(R).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072104/state.json" "file_sha256" "feecadad2d10121d0f138d6fc3adc9843b6280859d98f77c1bfc1cd903d32fc0"} {"question" "q-111807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072104/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bba728d73e286d9837877397aae3a7aace0726e78f07aa8edd9b1007daaab704"} {"question" "q-111807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072104/state.json" "file_sha256" "feecadad2d10121d0f138d6fc3adc9843b6280859d98f77c1bfc1cd903d32fc0"} {"question" "q-111807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-15"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "3"] ["text" "${{r}_{1},{r}_{2},{r}_{3}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(R)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072104/state.json" "file_sha256" "feecadad2d10121d0f138d6fc3adc9843b6280859d98f77c1bfc1cd903d32fc0"} {"question" "q-111807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${{r}_{1},{r}_